## INSPECTION KNOWLEDGE

### Pre-Roof Safety
- Check roof pitch BEFORE climbing
- Pitch > 6: Put on Cougar Paws boots, may need pitch hoppers
- Pitch < 4: NO shingles allowed — must use modified bitumen
- Re-check pitch on back of house — slope may change
- Pitch > 8/12: Steep slope charges apply, special equipment needed

### Hail Test Method
1. Mark a 10 ft x 10 ft test square with chalk
2. Count hail hits inside the square
3. Repeat for EACH slope direction of the house
4. Document with chalk marks and photos
5. Circle each hail hit with chalk — makes damage undeniable in photos
- State Farm threshold: ~10 hits per square
- Allstate threshold: ~15-20 hits per square

### Damage Indicators (Hail)
- Missing shingles
- Heavy granule loss on front and side slopes
- Dents in square roof vents
- Dents on gutter edges
- Cracked chimney crown
- Bad flashing around chimney
- Dry rotted pipe boots

### Chimney Rules
- If chimney wider than 24 inches: NEEDS A CRICKET
- Measure: width, depth, height
- Check crown (concrete top) for cracks
- Check mortar condition
- Check flashing condition

### RCRS Chimney Repair Process
1. Remove shingles around chimney
2. Remove existing flashing
3. Install ice and water shield directly on decking
4. Install new 4x4 flashing with hem
5. Install shingles
6. Install counter flashing cut into groove in brick
7. Install new metal chimney cap

### Measurements to Collect
- Roof pitch (front AND back — may differ)
- Chimney dimensions (width, depth, height)
- Pipe boot sizes
- Valley length estimate
- Roof age estimate
- Underlayment type
- Decking type
- Shingle type (architectural vs three-tab)
- Number of layers
- Linear feet of ridge, hip, and valley

### Measurement & Estimation
- 1 "square" = 100 square feet of roof area
- Typical residential roof: 20-40 squares
- Waste factor: 10-15% simple roof, 15-20% complex (hips, valleys, dormers)
- 3 bundles per square of shingles
- Standard crew (4-5 workers) installs 25-35 squares per day
- Always round UP when ordering materials
- EagleView for satellite measurements, verify on-site
- Tools: tape measure (25ft+), pitch gauge/speed square, chalk, camera

